{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ.</b> Rashi explained it as referring to all generations, but this is not elucidated in the verse. And it appears to me that since the Holy One, blessed be He, first showed Moses the pattern of the מִּשְׁכָּן, and afterward showed him the pattern of all its vessels, as it is written: ״אֵת תַּבְנִית הַמִּשְׁכָּן וְאֵת תַּבְנִית כָּל כֵּלָיו״ (Exodus 25:9). And when He commanded him concerning the makers of the work, He began with the vessels first, as it says: ״וְעָשׂוּ אֲרוֹן״ etc. (Exodus 25:10), and afterward He mentioned the מִּשְׁכָּן. And Moses would have been perplexed about this matter: should they make the מִּשְׁכָּן first according to the vision that he saw on the mountain and afterward the vessels, or should they make the vessels first according to the order in which they were mentioned in the command of making? Therefore it says ״וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ״ — with a vav, for had it said ״כֵּן תַּעֲשׂוּ״ (without the vav), I would have been compelled to say that it refers to the pattern of the מִּשְׁכָּן and its vessels and not to the order of precedence and sequence. But from the fact that it says ״וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ״, infer from it that before this the matter had been interrupted. And if so, surely what is stated — ״כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר אֲנִי מַרְאֶה אוֹתְךָ אֵת תַּבְנִית הַמִּשְׁכָּן וְאֵת תַּבְנִית כָּל כֵּלָיו״ — refers back to what was said above: ״וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ״ (Exodus 25:8). And if so, the making of their pattern is already stated, so what do I fulfill with ״וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ״? Rather, it means to say: in this order shall you make first the מִּשְׁכָּן and afterward its vessels. And as for the fact that He placed the אָרוֹן first, this is reckoning the order of the rank of their stature; and 'the last act in deed is the first in thought,' for the essential purpose of this building is for the sake of the אֲרוֹן בְּרִית ה׳, for there is the place of the שְׁכִינָה — therefore He placed it first. And I do not know who led Rashi into this difficulty, to say that Moses commanded Bezalel to make the vessels first, for we see the opposite of his words: behold, both in פָּרָשַׁת כִּי תִשָּׂא and in פָּרָשַׁת וַיַּקְהֵל, in every place He commanded concerning the מִּשְׁכָּן first. And if so, surely the fact that He placed the אָרוֹן first here is on account of its supremacy over the מִּשְׁכָּן and all its vessels. And who does not know in all this that the crown of Torah surpasses them all (Berakhot 55a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כֶּתֶר תּוֹרָה הוּא הָעוֹלֶה עַל כֻּלָּם' alludes to the Talmudic statement in Berakhot 55a that three crowns were given — of priesthood, of kingship, and of Torah — but the crown of Torah surpasses them all; the Kli Yakar applies this to the Ark, which represents Torah and is therefore mentioned first though built after the Mishkan."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:22:53.751561874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}